Third page PR of the silo.hllmr.com redesign, by Claude (Silo site). Request: [HLLMR/hllmr-infra#68](https://github.com/HLLMR/hllmr-infra/pull/68).

`/c/` is the one site URL compiled into every shipped Silo build (`collection.rs` `PAGE_BASE`: `/c/?g=<gist id>` and `/c/?r=<owner>/<repo>`). This PR moves it into the new site with that contract unchanged.

## What changes
- **`SharedSet.svelte`, rendered client-only at `/c/`:**
  - reads the set's `silo-collection.json` from GitHub in the visitor's browser, as before (already disclosed in the privacy policy);
  - shows the name, author, date, savegame and map, description and mod list;
  - hands off with the same deep link the old page used, `silo://collection?url=<ref>`, which the app's `parseCollectionDeepLink` accepts.
- **Stricter than the old page:**
  - the gist id, owner and repo are checked with the app's own rules (`github.rs`) before any request, so `?r=../etc` never reaches GitHub;
  - repo files are read through `api.github.com` with the raw media type;
  - a truncated gist is fetched only from `gist.githubusercontent.com`, which is added to `connect-src`;
  - all text renders as text, and documents over 1 MB are refused.
- **Clear failure states:** invalid link, deleted or private, not a Silo set, GitHub rate limit, and other errors.
- **Copy:** uses the app's "mod set" wording. It says nothing changes in your mods folder until you choose; that's the app's preview-first flow.
- **`PUBLIC_GITHUB_API`:** a bare origin, defaulting to `https://api.github.com`, so tests can point the page at `scripts/fixture-api.mjs`. That server now also serves `tests/fixtures/github/`.
- **URL contract:** the five `/c/` entries are live checks now (48 pass, 0 fail, 12 pending).

## Shared paths
`scripts/fixture-api.mjs` and `tests/fixtures/**` are in no release workflow's filter. Only release-silo fires (via `sites/silo/**`).

## Tests
- `npm test`: 129 files OK; html-validate clean; internal links 0 errors; contract 48/0/12.
- In the browser against real GitHub: a missing gist gives "isn't there any more"; `?g=not-a-gist` and `?r=../etc` give "doesn't look right" with no request made.
- In the browser against the fixtures (`PUBLIC_GITHUB_API=http://127.0.0.1:8787`):
  - a gist set and a repo set both render;
  - the deep links are exactly `silo://collection?url=0123…cdef` and `silo://collection?url=hllmr%2Fsilo-my-server-pack`;
  - a mod named `FS25_<script>…</script>` shows as text;
  - a wrong-schema file gives "isn't a Silo mod set";
  - at 375 px in dark theme there's no horizontal scroll.
- **Not tested:** clicking Open in Silo with the app installed. That's the app-side acceptance step, by the Silo developer or the owner, once this is live.

**Merge:** needs the owner's per-merge authorization, quoted here before merging with `--match-head-commit`.

