## Summary

- Replaces `docs/spec/block-simulation.md` with a specification in two parts:
  - **Part A**, an abstract contract: invariants, freedoms and instance parameters (`P-*`) that any implementation of the block simulation machinery chooses.
  - **Part B**, the vanilla instance in exact detail (`SIM-TICK`, `SIM-SET`, `SIM-NBR`, `SIM-SHP`, `SIM-SCH`, `SIM-BEV`, `SIM-RND`, `SIM-RNG`), and a rule-by-rule comparison with a threaded server.
- Checks the vanilla rules against the 26.4-snapshot-4 sources and corrects them. The main corrections:
  - a column starts to broadcast changes only after its transition to block-ticking completes;
  - the direct shape updates of pistons and shulker boxes, and their flags;
  - in a cascade with flags 3, only the first generation makes neighbor updates;
  - `/fill` loads the columns between its corners;
  - delay-1 ticks scheduled before the game time advance;
  - the overlap of random-tick picks at distances that are multiples of 32;
  - rain starts on the 20th tick, not the 21st.
- Adds section B.4, **intentional deviations**. Every instance of this project keeps the contract there instead of copying vanilla:
  - DEV-01: ticks lost or repeated at unload;
  - DEV-02: delay-1 ticks scheduled before the time advance;
  - DEV-03: duplicate saved ticks;
  - DEV-04: the stale "will tick this tick" group after an area clear;
  - DEV-05: column records with `UpgradeData`.

  Each deviation is `source_suggested`; DEV-01 has an experiment to confirm it.
- Adds guarantee levels to Part A (A.0): **exact**, **semantic** and **boundary**. Cross-partition messages are now explicitly the boundary level. They no longer conflict with the rule that a set returns only after its whole chain. OQ-12 answers the level of this project's instance: exact with one partition for each dimension, boundary (cross-partition messages in a stable order) with more. A semantic level across partitions would need a hand-over of sections mid-step; the spec records why the project does not build it. An item crosses a boundary when its target is outside the halo; message delivery must not depend on thread timing.
- Defines the halo: a step holds its halo exclusively, and the halo does not change during a step. The threaded instance discards cross-partition effects, so it is marked as a comparison, not a conforming instance.
- Tightens the parallel-execution contract:
  - conflicts cover every read/write case;
  - the rules, not the instance, fix the order of conflicting items; where the rules leave it free, a stable rule decides;
  - the footprint of a cascade grows as it runs;
  - when no collected tick is overdue, scheduled ticks keep (priority, sequence) order across sections, so repeater and comparator priorities hold across section boundaries.
- Makes SIM-MODEL-101 agree with SIM-SET-002 step 2.6: a set can fail after it already wrote its state.
- Adds the parameters `P-IDLE` (when an idle dimension stops entity and block entity ticks) and `P-CAPTURE` (the neighbor state of a queued shape update).
- Moves command behavior (`/setblock`, `/fill`, `/clone`) to an informative note for black-box experiments.
- Adds `docs/spec/README.md`, the writing rules for specifications in this directory: ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English, as this project adapts it. The block simulation specification follows these rules.

No code references the old rule text, so no other file changes.

## Test plan

- [ ] Read Part A and B.4 for the contract and the deviations.
- [ ] Spot-check the corrected rules against the cited behavior.

## Summary

After #16 the REC viewfinder video could only be set deep inside the long services form, under service 3 → Бүтээлүүд. That is very hard to find on a phone, and the owner couldn't find it.

**Үйлчилгээ & үнэ** now has a **🎬 REC видео** card right under the page title:

- pick a video (or an image), or remove it;
- optionally add the title shown under the video;
- **Хадгалаад нийтлэх** saves and publishes in one step.

The card writes the same field as the form (the video service's first work), so the two stay in sync. A note on the card explains that any other unpublished services edits are published at the same time. If no service uses the REC visual, the card explains how to set one.

## Testing

- At 390px:
  - opened Үйлчилгээ & үнэ, removed the video and picked a video in the media picker;
  - entered a title, then Хадгалаад нийтлэх;
  - the success toast appeared and the card reloaded with the video and title;
  - the home page then rendered `data-rec-video`;
  - no page errors.

