New plugin `berd` with `berd-contributing`. block/berd closes every PR from non-collaborators automatically (since 2026-08-14), so this skill is about filing the issue upstream actually wants and about building Berd on NixOS:

- the issues-only policy and what it means for a fix we need (a patch in our package, linked to the issue);
- the bug and feature forms field by field, the three bars (search, reproduce on the current release, one issue per issue), Linux log paths, scrubbing, the agent rules upstream enforces (human is the author, never invent details), and the nixpkgs angle to state (goose pinned to a main commit, managed ACP bridges via `npm ci` and a downloaded Node, telemetry and updater defaults, the macOS-only `catch` sidecar);
- building and validating on NixOS by change type (`just check` / `test` / `tauri-check` / `clippy` / `ci`), `GOOSE_BIN` as the override to test with nixpkgs' `goose-cli`;
- reading the codebase for a precise report: `LAWS/` as the source of truth, ACP as the main interface, berdctl invariants;
- how the team's own PRs look (titles, their `create-pr` and `code-review` skills, lefthook, Renovate, goose-pin bump PRs);
- what the history shows (289 PRs, 91 issues, 2026-08-12 to 2026-10-19): zero outside merges, internal median merge 1.3 h, 72 of 87 outside issues still open and mostly unlabeled, which reports got fixed within days and which ideas stall.

Also adds the goose row the README table was missing. `claude plugin validate .` passes (the usual no-version warnings).

